# motoquencer `buttoncolor` (`bc`), left at its default. motoquencer.md:967:
# "Set a user defined color for the gate buttons. This color is only used when
# buttonmode = 0." The firmware default is 0.1 -- the blue end of the colour
# ramp (basics.md 5.5: 0.0 dark, 0.2 cyan, and the hue line continued below the
# first named stop runs back towards blue), which is what the LED table's
# "blue | enabled gate | 0" row describes. So an unpatched `buttoncolor` paints
# 0.1, not the table's named blue 1.2.
#
# `F<n>.led` / `F<n>.color` read the step LED below motor fader n back
# (Engine::faderLed / faderLedColor). The played step is white regardless of
# buttonmode, which the engine encodes out of band as the negative sentinel -1.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock       = I1
    numsteps    = 4
    numfaders   = 4
    buttonmode  = 0
    defaultgate = 1
    cv          = O1
    gate        = O2
>>>
# Before the first clock there is no played step: all four gates paint 0.1.
@0 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F2.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F4.led 1 tol 1e-6
@0 expect F4.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
# Step 1 plays: lane 1 goes white, the others keep the gate colour.
@1 set I1 1
@1 expect F1.led 1 tol 1e-6
@1 expect F1.color -1 tol 1e-6
@1 expect F2.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@2 set I1 0
# Step 2 plays: lane 1 is back to the gate colour.
@3 set I1 1
@3 expect F1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
@3 expect F2.color -1 tol 1e-6
@4 set I1 0
# A gate-OFF step is dark in buttonmode 0 (plate 4 toggles step 4's gate off);
# step 2 is the played one, so lane 4 is free to show it.
@5 touch F4 1
@6 touch F4 0
@6 expect F4.led 0 tol 1e-6
@6 expect F4.color 0 tol 1e-6
@6 expect F1.color 0.1 tol 1e-6
